WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:09.352
Safe, elegant, fast. This is Osprey Agent on macOS: a real SwiftUI application, with application logic written in Osprey.

00:09.752 --> 00:17.901
This recorded calculator conversation starts with a precise request: run the tests, fix the package, and leave the tests unchanged.

00:18.301 --> 00:26.783
Open the activity group to inspect the commands and file reads. The first test run failed. The tool output is visible in the conversation.

00:27.183 --> 00:34.956
Now inspect the edit and the next command. Both tests pass. Scroll down to review the corrected code, with syntax highlighting.

00:40.183 --> 00:48.680
Scroll down to review the corrected code with syntax highlighting. The inspector keeps usage and changed files beside the conversation.

00:49.080 --> 01:03.182
These are real SwiftUI controls. Osprey application code compiles ahead of time through LLVM, without an embedded JavaScript engine. Typed effects put model requests and tools behind the host boundary.

01:03.282 --> 01:18.378
Build from the repository, then run make, dash C, apps slash macOS, agent, with PROJECT pointing to your folder. This agent is not sandboxed: it can run commands and change files your account can. Osprey is actively evolving.
